00:02:20.510 --> 00:02:23.660
about the performance of TPUs,
the TensorFlow Processing

00:02:23.660 --> 00:02:26.720
Units, and it has
a lot of detail.

00:02:26.720 --> 00:02:28.180
MARK MANDEL: It's super cool.

00:02:28.180 --> 00:02:31.050
The TensorFlow Processing
Units are custom chips

00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:34.335
for doing TensorFlow processing,
specifically for that task,

00:02:34.335 --> 00:02:35.210
and it's pretty cool.

00:02:35.210 --> 00:02:37.670
So we wrote a blog post about
the performance improvements

00:02:37.670 --> 00:02:41.090
we can see from running
workloads on sensor processing

00:02:41.090 --> 00:02:43.781
units versus GPUs
and against CPUs,

00:02:43.781 --> 00:02:46.030
and I'm going to read this
because I sound super cool.

00:02:46.030 --> 00:02:48.821
The TPU achieves better
energy efficiency

00:02:48.821 --> 00:02:49.820
than conventional chips.

00:02:49.820 --> 00:02:52.730
Achieving 30 to 80
times improvement

00:02:52.730 --> 00:02:55.880
in tera operations of
computation per watt of energy

00:02:55.880 --> 00:02:57.170
consumed.

00:02:57.170 --> 00:02:58.669
So basically it
does more for less.

00:02:58.669 --> 00:03:00.210
FRANCESC CAMPOY:
Yeah, it is amazing.

00:03:00.210 --> 00:03:04.280
There's a graph, that is not
the easiest graph to interpret,

00:03:04.280 --> 00:03:08.210
but basically it says how much
more performance you can get

00:03:08.210 --> 00:03:10.700
per watt in different systems.

00:03:10.700 --> 00:03:13.880
And basically we have two TPUs.

00:03:13.880 --> 00:03:19.040
The faster TPU achieves almost
200 times more performance

00:03:19.040 --> 00:03:23.660
per watt than a
CPU, which is a lot.

00:03:23.660 --> 00:03:26.060
So, definitely
worth it, especially

00:03:26.060 --> 00:03:27.740
if you're running TensorFlow.

00:03:27.740 --> 00:03:30.140
There's no better place
to process TensorFlow

00:03:30.140 --> 00:03:31.852
than in that TensorFlow
Processing Unit.

00:03:31.852 --> 00:03:33.560
